Exponent ledger
  Unit distance: Sawin gives planar sets with more than n^1.014 unit pairs.
  Carrier: high-degree algebraic number fields, small discriminant, many small-norm primes.
  Tournament max-H literature: max H(T) is Theta(n!/2^(n-1));
    Alon's upper-bound slack is polynomial n^(3/2), and random regular
    tournaments give constant-factor e asymptotics over the random baseline.
  Strong-tournament minimum HP literature has exponential base 5^(1/3),
    again not 1.014.
  S615 conclusion: the exact 1.014 is not yet a tournament theorem.
    Treat it as a target carrier-amplification exponent to search for in
    proof-obligation tournaments or arithmetic tournament carriers.

